window.CURRENT_TASK={"task_id": "L1-FUC-007-A6", "layer": "L1", "target_id": "FUC-007", "artifact_id": "FUC-007-A6", "title": "FUC-007 Publish Air and Surface Surveillance Tracks / A6", "protocol_version": "L1_final_semantic_verified_candidate_v2", "artifact_sha256": "746a8d349af7b9a445f4a2e6e6f46f3cd40a84d8be35829e29c0ef5c450e0f64", "source_sha256": "40e0827f373b73731838c63950f540172969d6c83af6ebea4de3c9f3f5722e99", "reference_sha256": null, "reference_origin": null, "instructions": "<pre>只依据本断言允许且实际提供的引用证据的并集判断，不使用其他页面或常识补充。entailment=所有实质内容获支持；contradiction=直接矛盾；neutral=有实质内容无支持且不矛盾。槽位适配独立判断。无合法引用填写 NO_VALID_CITATION，不得猜测支持。保留审计候选断言原边界，不用最终槽位代替。</pre>", "material_html": "<h3>Publish Air and Surface Surveillance Tracks</h3><p>给定参与者：C2 JU</p><p>按逐断言所列证据作答。最终槽位仅用于组织者计算 ESC；不替代审计候选。</p>", "groups": [{"key": "claims", "title": "逐断言评价", "fields": [{"key": "citation", "label": "引用状态", "type": "select", "required": true, "options": ["VALID", "NO_VALID_CITATION", "TECHNICAL_ISSUE"]}, {"key": "entailment", "label": "来源蕴含", "type": "select", "required": true, "options": ["entailment", "contradiction", "neutral", "NO_VALID_CITATION", "TECHNICAL_ISSUE"]}, {"key": "slot_fit", "label": "槽位适配", "type": "select", "required": true, "options": ["true", "false", "NOT_EVALUATED", "TECHNICAL_ISSUE"]}, {"key": "reason", "label": "证据判断理由", "type": "textarea", "required": true}, {"key": "slot_reason", "label": "槽位判断理由", "type": "textarea", "required": true}], "rows": [{"title": "goal:0", "html": "<pre>To originate and report real-time air and surface (maritime) tracks using the J3.2 and J3.3 surveillance messages.</pre><p>原引用：milstd6016b_sec4:P25#C70, milstd6016b_sec4:P23#C64；合法暴露引用：milstd6016b_sec4:P25#C70, milstd6016b_sec4:P23#C64</p><h4>证据 milstd6016b_sec4:P25#C70</h4><pre>The protocols in this section are to be followed in order to minimize occurrences and duration of dual designations.\nb. Each $\\mathrm { C } ^ { 2 }$ JU which has a capability to originate and report real-time air, surface (maritime), land (ground), or space tracks shall have a capability to perform common tracking in accordance with the correlation and decorrelation procedures and criteria which follow. The rules for correlation and decorrelation differ depending on the E/C of the tracks. The rules in paragraphs 4.4.4.3.1, 4.4.4.3.2, and 4.7.3 apply to the correlation and decorrelation of both air tracks and surface tracks, unless otherwise stated. The rules for correlation of land and space tracks are to be determined.\n4.4.4.3.1 AIR AND SURFACE TRACK CORRELATION</pre><p>原始页位置：[25]</p><h4>证据 milstd6016b_sec4:P23#C64</h4><pre>subfunctions are discussed within this subsection. Specific differences, when applicable, are included in the appropriate paragraphs.\nThe specific messages used to report Air, Surface (Maritime), and Land (Ground) surveillance data are the J3.2, J3.3, and J3.5 (PTI = 1) messages, respectively. These messages are monitored by nonC&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt; JUs, such as fighter aircraft, for situational awareness and early warning information.\nDiscussed in this subsection are the various requirements associated with Air, Surface (Maritime), and Land (Ground) surveillance data exchange. The topics covered are:\na. Track Reporting Criteria.\nb. Track Reporting.\nc. Track Correlation.\nd. Positional Data.\ne. Velocity.\nf. Identity/Identity Confidence/Strength.\ng. Transponder Data.\nh. Track Quality.\ni.</pre><p>原始页位置：[23]</p>"}, {"title": "preconditions:0", "html": "<pre>The C2 JU has an automatic correlation capability for air and surface tracks.</pre><p>原引用：milstd6016b_sec4:P25#C71；合法暴露引用：milstd6016b_sec4:P25#C71</p><h4>证据 milstd6016b_sec4:P25#C71</h4><pre>The correlation process commences with comparing locally derived sensor data (position, velocity, and altitude) with the data received on the interface, in order to prevent or eliminate dual designations. All $\\mathrm { C } ^ { 2 }$ JUs that originate real-time air or surface tracks shall have an automatic correlation capability. The following subparagraphs apply to the correlation of any two air tracks and any two surface tracks unless otherwise specified.\nMIL-STD-6016B\n4-171</pre><p>原始页位置：[25]</p>"}, {"title": "preconditions:1", "html": "<pre>The C2 JU has an automatic decorrelation capability for real-time air or surface tracks it initiates.</pre><p>原引用：milstd6016b_sec4:P39#C126；合法暴露引用：milstd6016b_sec4:P39#C126</p><h4>证据 milstd6016b_sec4:P39#C126</h4><pre>(d) Force Tell and Emergency Indicators. If the Dropped TN had the Force Tell Indicator set to value 1, the Retained TN shall have the Force Tell Indicator set to value 1. If the Dropped TN had the Emergency Indicator set to value 1, the Retained TN shall have the Emergency Indicator set to value 1.\n4.4.4.3.2 AIR AND SURFACE TRACK DECORRELATION\nThe following subparagraphs apply to the decorrelation of any two air tracks or any two surface tracks.\na. Decorrelation Requirements. All C&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt; JUs that initiate real-time air or surface tracks shall have an automatic decorrelation capability. C&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt; JUs may also perform manual decorrelation, and may have a capability to require manual confirmation of automatic decorrelations.</pre><p>原始页位置：[39]</p>"}, {"title": "preconditions:2", "html": "<pre>The C2 JU has the capability to perform common tracking in accordance with the correlation and decorrelation procedures and criteria.</pre><p>原引用：milstd6016b_sec4:P25#C70；合法暴露引用：milstd6016b_sec4:P25#C70</p><h4>证据 milstd6016b_sec4:P25#C70</h4><pre>The protocols in this section are to be followed in order to minimize occurrences and duration of dual designations.\nb. Each $\\mathrm { C } ^ { 2 }$ JU which has a capability to originate and report real-time air, surface (maritime), land (ground), or space tracks shall have a capability to perform common tracking in accordance with the correlation and decorrelation procedures and criteria which follow. The rules for correlation and decorrelation differ depending on the E/C of the tracks. The rules in paragraphs 4.4.4.3.1, 4.4.4.3.2, and 4.7.3 apply to the correlation and decorrelation of both air tracks and surface tracks, unless otherwise stated. The rules for correlation of land and space tracks are to be determined.\n4.4.4.3.1 AIR AND SURFACE TRACK CORRELATION</pre><p>原始页位置：[25]</p>"}, {"title": "preconditions:3", "html": "<pre>Sufficient reporting responsibility checks, correlation, and data registration have been performed.</pre><p>原引用：milstd6016b_sec4:P54#C179；合法暴露引用：milstd6016b_sec4:P54#C179</p><h4>证据 milstd6016b_sec4:P54#C179</h4><pre>4.4.4.17 MINIMUM WAIT BEFORE TRANSMITTING TRACKS\nAfter initially achieving Active status, or after returning to Active status from Inactive status or TDS Failure, $\\mathrm { C } ^ { 2 }$ JUs capable of assuming $\\mathtt { R } ^ { 2 }$ for air, surface, or land tracks shall not transmit air, surface, or land tracks until sufficient reporting responsibility checks, correlation, and data registration are performed (this also applies to a $\\mathrm { C } ^ { 2 }$ JU that is deactivating a receive filter). The minimum wait before reporting air and surface tracks is 12 seconds and for land tracks is 48 seconds. This may be either an automatic or manual function.</pre><p>原始页位置：[54]</p>"}, {"title": "preconditions:4", "html": "<pre>After initially achieving Active status or returning to Active status from Inactive status or TDS Failure, the minimum wait of 12 seconds before reporting air and surface tracks has elapsed.</pre><p>原引用：milstd6016b_sec4:P54#C179；合法暴露引用：milstd6016b_sec4:P54#C179</p><h4>证据 milstd6016b_sec4:P54#C179</h4><pre>4.4.4.17 MINIMUM WAIT BEFORE TRANSMITTING TRACKS\nAfter initially achieving Active status, or after returning to Active status from Inactive status or TDS Failure, $\\mathrm { C } ^ { 2 }$ JUs capable of assuming $\\mathtt { R } ^ { 2 }$ for air, surface, or land tracks shall not transmit air, surface, or land tracks until sufficient reporting responsibility checks, correlation, and data registration are performed (this also applies to a $\\mathrm { C } ^ { 2 }$ JU that is deactivating a receive filter). The minimum wait before reporting air and surface tracks is 12 seconds and for land tracks is 48 seconds. This may be either an automatic or manual function.</pre><p>原始页位置：[54]</p>"}, {"title": "trigger:0", "html": "<pre>A C2 JU initiates a real-time air or surface track.</pre><p>原引用：milstd6016b_sec4:P39#C126, milstd6016b_sec4:P25#C70；合法暴露引用：milstd6016b_sec4:P39#C126, milstd6016b_sec4:P25#C70</p><h4>证据 milstd6016b_sec4:P39#C126</h4><pre>(d) Force Tell and Emergency Indicators. If the Dropped TN had the Force Tell Indicator set to value 1, the Retained TN shall have the Force Tell Indicator set to value 1. If the Dropped TN had the Emergency Indicator set to value 1, the Retained TN shall have the Emergency Indicator set to value 1.\n4.4.4.3.2 AIR AND SURFACE TRACK DECORRELATION\nThe following subparagraphs apply to the decorrelation of any two air tracks or any two surface tracks.\na. Decorrelation Requirements. All C&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt; JUs that initiate real-time air or surface tracks shall have an automatic decorrelation capability. C&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt; JUs may also perform manual decorrelation, and may have a capability to require manual confirmation of automatic decorrelations.</pre><p>原始页位置：[39]</p><h4>证据 milstd6016b_sec4:P25#C70</h4><pre>The protocols in this section are to be followed in order to minimize occurrences and duration of dual designations.\nb. Each $\\mathrm { C } ^ { 2 }$ JU which has a capability to originate and report real-time air, surface (maritime), land (ground), or space tracks shall have a capability to perform common tracking in accordance with the correlation and decorrelation procedures and criteria which follow. The rules for correlation and decorrelation differ depending on the E/C of the tracks. The rules in paragraphs 4.4.4.3.1, 4.4.4.3.2, and 4.7.3 apply to the correlation and decorrelation of both air tracks and surface tracks, unless otherwise stated. The rules for correlation of land and space tracks are to be determined.\n4.4.4.3.1 AIR AND SURFACE TRACK CORRELATION</pre><p>原始页位置：[25]</p>"}, {"title": "main_flow:0", "html": "<pre>The C2 JU, having the capability to originate and report real-time air or surface tracks, performs common tracking in accordance with the correlation and decorrelation procedures and criteria.</pre><p>原引用：milstd6016b_sec4:P25#C70；合法暴露引用：milstd6016b_sec4:P25#C70</p><h4>证据 milstd6016b_sec4:P25#C70</h4><pre>The protocols in this section are to be followed in order to minimize occurrences and duration of dual designations.\nb. Each $\\mathrm { C } ^ { 2 }$ JU which has a capability to originate and report real-time air, surface (maritime), land (ground), or space tracks shall have a capability to perform common tracking in accordance with the correlation and decorrelation procedures and criteria which follow. The rules for correlation and decorrelation differ depending on the E/C of the tracks. The rules in paragraphs 4.4.4.3.1, 4.4.4.3.2, and 4.7.3 apply to the correlation and decorrelation of both air tracks and surface tracks, unless otherwise stated. The rules for correlation of land and space tracks are to be determined.\n4.4.4.3.1 AIR AND SURFACE TRACK CORRELATION</pre><p>原始页位置：[25]</p>"}, {"title": "main_flow:1", "html": "<pre>In common tracking, the C2 JU shares a common track number and shifting R^2 between C2 JUs; each air, surface (maritime), land (ground), and space tracked object is normally reported by one C2 JU while other C2 JUs withhold their reports to prevent cluttering the tactical plot.</pre><p>原引用：milstd6016b_sec4:P25#C68；合法暴露引用：milstd6016b_sec4:P25#C68</p><h4>证据 milstd6016b_sec4:P25#C68</h4><pre>4.4.4.3 COMMON TRACKING\na. Common tracking is defined as sharing of a common track number and shifting $\\mathbb { R } ^ { 2 }$ between $\\mathrm { C } ^ { 2 }$ JUs. Each air, surface (maritime), land (ground), and space tracked object normally will be reported by one $\\mathrm { C } ^ { 2 }$ JU while other $\\mathrm { C } ^ { 2 }$ JUs withhold their reports to prevent cluttering the tactical plot. Determination of the $\\mathrm { C } ^ { 2 }$ JU responsible for reporting the tracked object shall be in accordance with the procedures in the Air, Surface, Land, and Space Surveillance sections. In this section and in section 4.7.3, Resolution of Air and Surface Track Dual Designations,</pre><p>原始页位置：[25]</p>"}, {"title": "main_flow:2", "html": "<pre>The C2 JU commences the correlation process by comparing locally derived sensor data (position, velocity, and altitude) with data received on the interface to prevent or eliminate dual designations.</pre><p>原引用：milstd6016b_sec4:P25#C71；合法暴露引用：milstd6016b_sec4:P25#C71</p><h4>证据 milstd6016b_sec4:P25#C71</h4><pre>The correlation process commences with comparing locally derived sensor data (position, velocity, and altitude) with the data received on the interface, in order to prevent or eliminate dual designations. All $\\mathrm { C } ^ { 2 }$ JUs that originate real-time air or surface tracks shall have an automatic correlation capability. The following subparagraphs apply to the correlation of any two air tracks and any two surface tracks unless otherwise specified.\nMIL-STD-6016B\n4-171</pre><p>原始页位置：[25]</p>"}, {"title": "main_flow:3", "html": "<pre>The C2 JU periodically compares remote tracks to local tracks (and, optionally, to common local tracks) to determine if a dual designation has occurred.</pre><p>原引用：milstd6016b_sec4:P113#C379；合法暴露引用：milstd6016b_sec4:P113#C379</p><h4>证据 milstd6016b_sec4:P113#C379</h4><pre>4.7.3 RESOLUTION OF AIR AND SURFACE TRACK DUAL DESIGNATIONS\na. The recognition and resolution of dual designations require all IUs\nto periodically compare remote tracks to local tracks (and, optionally, to\ncommon local tracks) to determine if a dual designation has occurred. The\nfrequency of such comparisons the criteria for determining that two tracks\nrepresent the same object, and the correlation rules shall be in accordance\nwith section 4.4.4.3.1, Air and Surface Track Correlation. The rules for\nland (ground) and space track dual designation resolution are TBD.\nb. When a $\\mathrm { C } ^ { 2 }$ JU recognizes that two tracks which are being reported to\nthe interface are eligible for correlation, that JU shall initiate action,\neither automatically or manually,</pre><p>原始页位置：[113]</p>"}, {"title": "main_flow:4", "html": "<pre>When the C2 JU recognizes that two tracks being reported to the interface are eligible for correlation, it initiates action, either automatically or manually.</pre><p>原引用：milstd6016b_sec4:P113#C379；合法暴露引用：milstd6016b_sec4:P113#C379</p><h4>证据 milstd6016b_sec4:P113#C379</h4><pre>4.7.3 RESOLUTION OF AIR AND SURFACE TRACK DUAL DESIGNATIONS\na. The recognition and resolution of dual designations require all IUs\nto periodically compare remote tracks to local tracks (and, optionally, to\ncommon local tracks) to determine if a dual designation has occurred. The\nfrequency of such comparisons the criteria for determining that two tracks\nrepresent the same object, and the correlation rules shall be in accordance\nwith section 4.4.4.3.1, Air and Surface Track Correlation. The rules for\nland (ground) and space track dual designation resolution are TBD.\nb. When a $\\mathrm { C } ^ { 2 }$ JU recognizes that two tracks which are being reported to\nthe interface are eligible for correlation, that JU shall initiate action,\neither automatically or manually,</pre><p>原始页位置：[113]</p>"}, {"title": "main_flow:5", "html": "<pre>The C2 JU reports Air surveillance data using the J3.2 (PTI = 1) message and Surface (Maritime) surveillance data using the J3.3 (PTI = 1) message.</pre><p>原引用：milstd6016b_sec4:P23#C64；合法暴露引用：milstd6016b_sec4:P23#C64</p><h4>证据 milstd6016b_sec4:P23#C64</h4><pre>subfunctions are discussed within this subsection. Specific differences, when applicable, are included in the appropriate paragraphs.\nThe specific messages used to report Air, Surface (Maritime), and Land (Ground) surveillance data are the J3.2, J3.3, and J3.5 (PTI = 1) messages, respectively. These messages are monitored by nonC&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt; JUs, such as fighter aircraft, for situational awareness and early warning information.\nDiscussed in this subsection are the various requirements associated with Air, Surface (Maritime), and Land (Ground) surveillance data exchange. The topics covered are:\na. Track Reporting Criteria.\nb. Track Reporting.\nc. Track Correlation.\nd. Positional Data.\ne. Velocity.\nf. Identity/Identity Confidence/Strength.\ng. Transponder Data.\nh. Track Quality.\ni.</pre><p>原始页位置：[23]</p>"}, {"title": "main_flow:6", "html": "<pre>For Air surveillance reporting, the C2 JU includes Altitude and Altitude Source when available.</pre><p>原引用：milstd6016b_sec4:P41#C133；合法暴露引用：milstd6016b_sec4:P41#C133</p><h4>证据 milstd6016b_sec4:P41#C133</h4><pre>Surface (Maritime), and Land (Ground) Point/Track messages. In addition, Air surveillance reporting shall include Altitude and Altitude Source when available.\n4.4.4.5 VARIANCE AND TIME STAMP ON NEEDLINE PGs\nThe J12.6C7 Kinematic Data 1 continuation word is used by nonC&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt; JUs on Needline PGs to report kinematics estimated errors on the track when it is necessary to have more accurate data than the target position quality indicator.\n4.4.4.5.1 VARIANCE EVALUATION ON NEEDLINE PGs\nThe estimation of error is needed independently on each measurement axis. For instance for a BEARING, ELEVATION, and DISTANCE independent measurement and estimation, the variance of error in bearing, elevation and distance is required.</pre><p>原始页位置：[41]</p>"}, {"title": "main_flow:7", "html": "<pre>The C2 JU reports the velocity of Air and Surface (Maritime) tracks as course and speed, with speed reported in data miles per hour of ground speed and course reported in degrees with respect to true north.</pre><p>原引用：milstd6016b_sec4:P43#C138；合法暴露引用：milstd6016b_sec4:P43#C138</p><h4>证据 milstd6016b_sec4:P43#C138</h4><pre>cannot be better than 500 ms, a NO STATEMENT shall be set in the HUNDREDTHS field. In case the accuracy cannot be better than a minute, a NO STATEMENT shall be set in the SECOND field.\n4.4.4.6 VELOCITY\nThe velocity of Air, Surface (Maritime), and Land (Ground) tracks shall be reported as course and speed. The speed shall be reported in data miles per hour of ground speed. The course shall be reported in degrees with respect to true north.\n4.4.4.7 IDENTITY DATA\nTrack identity as defined in paragraph 4.4.2.1 is exchanged. The platform and platform activity fields are defined in the message section of this volume.\nFor each of the Platform, Platform Activity, Specific Type, and Special Interest Indicator fields which are implemented by a C&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt; JU,</pre><p>原始页位置：[43]</p>"}, {"title": "main_flow:8", "html": "<pre>The C2 JU exchanges track identity as defined in paragraph 4.4.2.1.</pre><p>原引用：milstd6016b_sec4:P43#C138；合法暴露引用：milstd6016b_sec4:P43#C138</p><h4>证据 milstd6016b_sec4:P43#C138</h4><pre>cannot be better than 500 ms, a NO STATEMENT shall be set in the HUNDREDTHS field. In case the accuracy cannot be better than a minute, a NO STATEMENT shall be set in the SECOND field.\n4.4.4.6 VELOCITY\nThe velocity of Air, Surface (Maritime), and Land (Ground) tracks shall be reported as course and speed. The speed shall be reported in data miles per hour of ground speed. The course shall be reported in degrees with respect to true north.\n4.4.4.7 IDENTITY DATA\nTrack identity as defined in paragraph 4.4.2.1 is exchanged. The platform and platform activity fields are defined in the message section of this volume.\nFor each of the Platform, Platform Activity, Specific Type, and Special Interest Indicator fields which are implemented by a C&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt; JU,</pre><p>原始页位置：[43]</p>"}, {"title": "alternative_flow:0", "html": "<pre>At main flow step 0, the C2 JU may also perform manual decorrelation, and may have a capability to require manual confirmation of automatic decorrelations.</pre><p>原引用：milstd6016b_sec4:P39#C126；合法暴露引用：milstd6016b_sec4:P39#C126</p><h4>证据 milstd6016b_sec4:P39#C126</h4><pre>(d) Force Tell and Emergency Indicators. If the Dropped TN had the Force Tell Indicator set to value 1, the Retained TN shall have the Force Tell Indicator set to value 1. If the Dropped TN had the Emergency Indicator set to value 1, the Retained TN shall have the Emergency Indicator set to value 1.\n4.4.4.3.2 AIR AND SURFACE TRACK DECORRELATION\nThe following subparagraphs apply to the decorrelation of any two air tracks or any two surface tracks.\na. Decorrelation Requirements. All C&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt; JUs that initiate real-time air or surface tracks shall have an automatic decorrelation capability. C&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt; JUs may also perform manual decorrelation, and may have a capability to require manual confirmation of automatic decorrelations.</pre><p>原始页位置：[39]</p>"}, {"title": "alternative_flow:1", "html": "<pre>At main flow step 4, if a correlation request is rejected, the C2 JU transmits the J7.2 message with the RV field set to value 2 to report the rejection. When the RV field is set to value 3, it indicates the correlation was manually initiated and shall be accepted unless certain conditions apply which require rejection.</pre><p>原引用：milstd6016b_sec4:P113#C381；合法暴露引用：milstd6016b_sec4:P113#C381</p><h4>证据 milstd6016b_sec4:P113#C381</h4><pre>value 1 it indicates a reverse correlation request would be rejected.\nReceiving IUs desiring to reverse the requested correlation use the RV field\nto determine if a reverse correlation request should be originated or if the\noriginal correlation request should be rejected. Whenever a correlation\nrequest is rejected the J7.2 message with the RV field set to value 2 shall\nbe transmitted to report the rejection. When the RV field is set to value 3,\nit indicates the correlation was manually initiated and shall be accepted\nunless certain conditions apply which require rejection (see paragraph\n4.7.3.2.c). The rules for the resolution of dual designations are provided\nin the following paragraphs.\nc. All $\\mathrm { C } ^ { 2 }$ JUs capable of reporting air or surface tracks shall have the</pre><p>原始页位置：[113]</p>"}, {"title": "alternative_flow:2", "html": "<pre>At main flow step 5, if the C2 JU does not have R^2, it is responsible for monitoring IFF/SIF surveillance data and only reporting if it holds different data with the J7.5 message; the JU with R^2 reports all IFF/SIF valid data locally held for that track in accordance with the transmit rules for the J3 messages.</pre><p>原引用：milstd6016b_sec4:P47#C154；合法暴露引用：milstd6016b_sec4:P47#C154</p><h4>证据 milstd6016b_sec4:P47#C154</h4><pre>4.4.4.9.1 IFF/SIF SURVEILLANCE DATA REPORTING\nThe reporting of IFF/SIF surveillance data in the J3.2C1 and J3.3C1 words for\nAir and Surface tracks, respectively, is the responsibility of the JU with $\\mathtt { R } ^ { 2 }$\nwhile all other JUs without $\\mathtt { R } ^ { 2 }$ are responsible for monitoring such data and\nonly reporting if they hold different data with the J7.5 message. In this\nway the JU with $\\mathtt { R } ^ { 2 }$ can be assumed to be reporting the most current data\navailable in the interface. Surveillance reporting rules are as follows:\na. $\\mathtt { R } ^ { 2 }$ units shall report all IFF/SIF valid data locally held for that\ntrack in accordance with the transmit rules for the J3 messages. Validity of</pre><p>原始页位置：[47]</p>"}, {"title": "alternative_flow:3", "html": "<pre>At main flow step 5, if the C2 JU ceases reporting a track for which it currently has R^2, it transmits the J7.0 (ACT = 0) message, except when it ceases reporting because it has relinquished R^2 to another JU or when that track becomes an Active IU on the network with the same TN.</pre><p>原引用：milstd6016b_sec4:P53#C177；合法暴露引用：milstd6016b_sec4:P53#C177</p><h4>证据 milstd6016b_sec4:P53#C177</h4><pre>4.4.4.15.1 SURVEILLANCE DATA DIFFERENCE (POSITION/VELOCITY/ALTITUDE OR ELEVATION)\n4.4.4.16 TERMINATION OF AIR, SURFACE (MARITIME), AND LAND (GROUND) TRACK DATA\nThe following subparagraphs describe the termination of Air, Surface (Maritime), and Land (Ground) tracks.\n4.4.4.16.1 TRANSMISSION OF THE DROP TRACK REPORT MESSAGE\nThe J7.0 (ACT = 0) message is transmitted when a JU ceases reporting a track for which it currently has R&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt;, except in the following cases:\na. When a JU ceases reporting a track because it has relinquished $\\mathtt { R } ^ { 2 }$ to another JU.\nb. When that track becomes an Active IU on the network with the same TN.\n4.4.4.16.2 PURGING OF REMOTE TRACKS\nThere may be cases when a system does not receive a J7.</pre><p>原始页位置：[53]</p>"}, {"title": "exception_flow:0", "html": "<pre>If a correlation request is rejected, the J7.2 message with the RV field set to value 2 shall be transmitted to report the rejection. Exit: the rejection is reported via J7.2.</pre><p>原引用：milstd6016b_sec4:P113#C381；合法暴露引用：milstd6016b_sec4:P113#C381</p><h4>证据 milstd6016b_sec4:P113#C381</h4><pre>value 1 it indicates a reverse correlation request would be rejected.\nReceiving IUs desiring to reverse the requested correlation use the RV field\nto determine if a reverse correlation request should be originated or if the\noriginal correlation request should be rejected. Whenever a correlation\nrequest is rejected the J7.2 message with the RV field set to value 2 shall\nbe transmitted to report the rejection. When the RV field is set to value 3,\nit indicates the correlation was manually initiated and shall be accepted\nunless certain conditions apply which require rejection (see paragraph\n4.7.3.2.c). The rules for the resolution of dual designations are provided\nin the following paragraphs.\nc. All $\\mathrm { C } ^ { 2 }$ JUs capable of reporting air or surface tracks shall have the</pre><p>原始页位置：[113]</p>"}, {"title": "exception_flow:1", "html": "<pre>After initially achieving Active status, or after returning to Active status from Inactive status or TDS Failure, C2 JUs capable of assuming R^2 for air, surface, or land tracks shall not transmit air, surface, or land tracks until sufficient reporting responsibility checks, correlation, and data registration are performed; the minimum wait before reporting air and surface tracks is 12 seconds. Exit: transmission is withheld until those checks and the minimum wait are complete.</pre><p>原引用：milstd6016b_sec4:P54#C179；合法暴露引用：milstd6016b_sec4:P54#C179</p><h4>证据 milstd6016b_sec4:P54#C179</h4><pre>4.4.4.17 MINIMUM WAIT BEFORE TRANSMITTING TRACKS\nAfter initially achieving Active status, or after returning to Active status from Inactive status or TDS Failure, $\\mathrm { C } ^ { 2 }$ JUs capable of assuming $\\mathtt { R } ^ { 2 }$ for air, surface, or land tracks shall not transmit air, surface, or land tracks until sufficient reporting responsibility checks, correlation, and data registration are performed (this also applies to a $\\mathrm { C } ^ { 2 }$ JU that is deactivating a receive filter). The minimum wait before reporting air and surface tracks is 12 seconds and for land tracks is 48 seconds. This may be either an automatic or manual function.</pre><p>原始页位置：[54]</p>"}, {"title": "exception_flow:2", "html": "<pre>For IFF/SIF surveillance data reporting, all JUs without R^2 are responsible for monitoring such data and only reporting if they hold different data with the J7.5 message. Exit: if different data are held, report them with J7.5; otherwise continue monitoring and do not report.</pre><p>原引用：milstd6016b_sec4:P47#C154；合法暴露引用：milstd6016b_sec4:P47#C154</p><h4>证据 milstd6016b_sec4:P47#C154</h4><pre>4.4.4.9.1 IFF/SIF SURVEILLANCE DATA REPORTING\nThe reporting of IFF/SIF surveillance data in the J3.2C1 and J3.3C1 words for\nAir and Surface tracks, respectively, is the responsibility of the JU with $\\mathtt { R } ^ { 2 }$\nwhile all other JUs without $\\mathtt { R } ^ { 2 }$ are responsible for monitoring such data and\nonly reporting if they hold different data with the J7.5 message. In this\nway the JU with $\\mathtt { R } ^ { 2 }$ can be assumed to be reporting the most current data\navailable in the interface. Surveillance reporting rules are as follows:\na. $\\mathtt { R } ^ { 2 }$ units shall report all IFF/SIF valid data locally held for that\ntrack in accordance with the transmit rules for the J3 messages. Validity of</pre><p>原始页位置：[47]</p>"}, {"title": "postconditions:0", "html": "<pre>Air surveillance data is reported using the J3.2 (PTI = 1) message.</pre><p>原引用：milstd6016b_sec4:P23#C64；合法暴露引用：milstd6016b_sec4:P23#C64</p><h4>证据 milstd6016b_sec4:P23#C64</h4><pre>subfunctions are discussed within this subsection. Specific differences, when applicable, are included in the appropriate paragraphs.\nThe specific messages used to report Air, Surface (Maritime), and Land (Ground) surveillance data are the J3.2, J3.3, and J3.5 (PTI = 1) messages, respectively. These messages are monitored by nonC&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt; JUs, such as fighter aircraft, for situational awareness and early warning information.\nDiscussed in this subsection are the various requirements associated with Air, Surface (Maritime), and Land (Ground) surveillance data exchange. The topics covered are:\na. Track Reporting Criteria.\nb. Track Reporting.\nc. Track Correlation.\nd. Positional Data.\ne. Velocity.\nf. Identity/Identity Confidence/Strength.\ng. Transponder Data.\nh. Track Quality.\ni.</pre><p>原始页位置：[23]</p>"}, {"title": "postconditions:1", "html": "<pre>Surface (Maritime) surveillance data is reported using the J3.3 (PTI = 1) message.</pre><p>原引用：milstd6016b_sec4:P23#C64；合法暴露引用：milstd6016b_sec4:P23#C64</p><h4>证据 milstd6016b_sec4:P23#C64</h4><pre>subfunctions are discussed within this subsection. Specific differences, when applicable, are included in the appropriate paragraphs.\nThe specific messages used to report Air, Surface (Maritime), and Land (Ground) surveillance data are the J3.2, J3.3, and J3.5 (PTI = 1) messages, respectively. These messages are monitored by nonC&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt; JUs, such as fighter aircraft, for situational awareness and early warning information.\nDiscussed in this subsection are the various requirements associated with Air, Surface (Maritime), and Land (Ground) surveillance data exchange. The topics covered are:\na. Track Reporting Criteria.\nb. Track Reporting.\nc. Track Correlation.\nd. Positional Data.\ne. Velocity.\nf. Identity/Identity Confidence/Strength.\ng. Transponder Data.\nh. Track Quality.\ni.</pre><p>原始页位置：[23]</p>"}, {"title": "postconditions:2", "html": "<pre>Air surveillance reporting includes Altitude and Altitude Source when available.</pre><p>原引用：milstd6016b_sec4:P41#C133；合法暴露引用：milstd6016b_sec4:P41#C133</p><h4>证据 milstd6016b_sec4:P41#C133</h4><pre>Surface (Maritime), and Land (Ground) Point/Track messages. In addition, Air surveillance reporting shall include Altitude and Altitude Source when available.\n4.4.4.5 VARIANCE AND TIME STAMP ON NEEDLINE PGs\nThe J12.6C7 Kinematic Data 1 continuation word is used by nonC&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt; JUs on Needline PGs to report kinematics estimated errors on the track when it is necessary to have more accurate data than the target position quality indicator.\n4.4.4.5.1 VARIANCE EVALUATION ON NEEDLINE PGs\nThe estimation of error is needed independently on each measurement axis. For instance for a BEARING, ELEVATION, and DISTANCE independent measurement and estimation, the variance of error in bearing, elevation and distance is required.</pre><p>原始页位置：[41]</p>"}, {"title": "postconditions:3", "html": "<pre>The velocity of Air and Surface (Maritime) tracks is reported as course and speed, with speed reported in data miles per hour of ground speed and course reported in degrees with respect to true north.</pre><p>原引用：milstd6016b_sec4:P43#C138；合法暴露引用：milstd6016b_sec4:P43#C138</p><h4>证据 milstd6016b_sec4:P43#C138</h4><pre>cannot be better than 500 ms, a NO STATEMENT shall be set in the HUNDREDTHS field. In case the accuracy cannot be better than a minute, a NO STATEMENT shall be set in the SECOND field.\n4.4.4.6 VELOCITY\nThe velocity of Air, Surface (Maritime), and Land (Ground) tracks shall be reported as course and speed. The speed shall be reported in data miles per hour of ground speed. The course shall be reported in degrees with respect to true north.\n4.4.4.7 IDENTITY DATA\nTrack identity as defined in paragraph 4.4.2.1 is exchanged. The platform and platform activity fields are defined in the message section of this volume.\nFor each of the Platform, Platform Activity, Specific Type, and Special Interest Indicator fields which are implemented by a C&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt; JU,</pre><p>原始页位置：[43]</p>"}, {"title": "postconditions:4", "html": "<pre>Track identity is exchanged as defined in paragraph 4.4.2.1.</pre><p>原引用：milstd6016b_sec4:P43#C138；合法暴露引用：milstd6016b_sec4:P43#C138</p><h4>证据 milstd6016b_sec4:P43#C138</h4><pre>cannot be better than 500 ms, a NO STATEMENT shall be set in the HUNDREDTHS field. In case the accuracy cannot be better than a minute, a NO STATEMENT shall be set in the SECOND field.\n4.4.4.6 VELOCITY\nThe velocity of Air, Surface (Maritime), and Land (Ground) tracks shall be reported as course and speed. The speed shall be reported in data miles per hour of ground speed. The course shall be reported in degrees with respect to true north.\n4.4.4.7 IDENTITY DATA\nTrack identity as defined in paragraph 4.4.2.1 is exchanged. The platform and platform activity fields are defined in the message section of this volume.\nFor each of the Platform, Platform Activity, Specific Type, and Special Interest Indicator fields which are implemented by a C&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt; JU,</pre><p>原始页位置：[43]</p>"}], "repeat": false, "min_rows": 0}], "blockers": [], "claim_meta": [{"slot": "goal", "audit_ordinal": 0, "content": "To originate and report real-time air and surface (maritime) tracks using the J3.2 and J3.3 surveillance messages.", "authored_evidence_refs": ["milstd6016b_sec4:P25#C70", "milstd6016b_sec4:P23#C64"], "exposed_evidence_refs": ["milstd6016b_sec4:P39#C126", "milstd6016b_sec4:P41#C133", "milstd6016b_sec4:P113#C381", "milstd6016b_sec4:P43#C138", "milstd6016b_sec4:P113#C379", "milstd6016b_sec4:P23#C64", "milstd6016b_sec4:P25#C70", "milstd6016b_sec4:P25#C71", "milstd6016b_sec4:P54#C179", "milstd6016b_sec4:P53#C177"], "valid_citation": true}, {"slot": "preconditions", "audit_ordinal": 0, "content": "The C2 JU has an automatic correlation capability for air and surface tracks.", "authored_evidence_refs": ["milstd6016b_sec4:P25#C71"], "exposed_evidence_refs": ["milstd6016b_sec4:P39#C126", "milstd6016b_sec4:P23#C64", "milstd6016b_sec4:P25#C70", "milstd6016b_sec4:P113#C381", "milstd6016b_sec4:P113#C379", "milstd6016b_sec4:P54#C179", "milstd6016b_sec4:P25#C71", "milstd6016b_sec4:P43#C138", "milstd6016b_sec4:P47#C154", "milstd6016b_sec4:P41#C133"], "valid_citation": true}, {"slot": "preconditions", "audit_ordinal": 1, "content": "The C2 JU has an automatic decorrelation capability for real-time air or surface tracks it initiates.", "authored_evidence_refs": ["milstd6016b_sec4:P39#C126"], "exposed_evidence_refs": ["milstd6016b_sec4:P39#C126", "milstd6016b_sec4:P23#C64", "milstd6016b_sec4:P25#C70", "milstd6016b_sec4:P113#C381", "milstd6016b_sec4:P113#C379", "milstd6016b_sec4:P54#C179", "milstd6016b_sec4:P25#C71", "milstd6016b_sec4:P43#C138", "milstd6016b_sec4:P47#C154", "milstd6016b_sec4:P41#C133"], "valid_citation": true}, {"slot": "preconditions", "audit_ordinal": 2, "content": "The C2 JU has the capability to perform common tracking in accordance with the correlation and decorrelation procedures and criteria.", "authored_evidence_refs": ["milstd6016b_sec4:P25#C70"], "exposed_evidence_refs": ["milstd6016b_sec4:P39#C126", "milstd6016b_sec4:P23#C64", "milstd6016b_sec4:P25#C70", "milstd6016b_sec4:P113#C381", "milstd6016b_sec4:P113#C379", "milstd6016b_sec4:P54#C179", "milstd6016b_sec4:P25#C71", "milstd6016b_sec4:P43#C138", "milstd6016b_sec4:P47#C154", "milstd6016b_sec4:P41#C133"], "valid_citation": true}, {"slot": "preconditions", "audit_ordinal": 3, "content": "Sufficient reporting responsibility checks, correlation, and data registration have been performed.", "authored_evidence_refs": ["milstd6016b_sec4:P54#C179"], "exposed_evidence_refs": ["milstd6016b_sec4:P39#C126", "milstd6016b_sec4:P23#C64", "milstd6016b_sec4:P25#C70", "milstd6016b_sec4:P113#C381", "milstd6016b_sec4:P113#C379", "milstd6016b_sec4:P54#C179", "milstd6016b_sec4:P25#C71", "milstd6016b_sec4:P43#C138", "milstd6016b_sec4:P47#C154", "milstd6016b_sec4:P41#C133"], "valid_citation": true}, {"slot": "preconditions", "audit_ordinal": 4, "content": "After initially achieving Active status or returning to Active status from Inactive status or TDS Failure, the minimum wait of 12 seconds before reporting air and surface tracks has elapsed.", "authored_evidence_refs": ["milstd6016b_sec4:P54#C179"], "exposed_evidence_refs": ["milstd6016b_sec4:P39#C126", "milstd6016b_sec4:P23#C64", "milstd6016b_sec4:P25#C70", "milstd6016b_sec4:P113#C381", "milstd6016b_sec4:P113#C379", "milstd6016b_sec4:P54#C179", "milstd6016b_sec4:P25#C71", "milstd6016b_sec4:P43#C138", "milstd6016b_sec4:P47#C154", "milstd6016b_sec4:P41#C133"], "valid_citation": true}, {"slot": "trigger", "audit_ordinal": 0, "content": "A C2 JU initiates a real-time air or surface track.", "authored_evidence_refs": ["milstd6016b_sec4:P39#C126", "milstd6016b_sec4:P25#C70"], "exposed_evidence_refs": ["milstd6016b_sec4:P39#C126", "milstd6016b_sec4:P113#C381", "milstd6016b_sec4:P113#C379", "milstd6016b_sec4:P25#C71", "milstd6016b_sec4:P23#C64", "milstd6016b_sec4:P41#C133", "milstd6016b_sec4:P53#C177", "milstd6016b_sec4:P25#C70", "milstd6016b_sec4:P43#C138", "milstd6016b_sec4:P46#C148"], "valid_citation": true}, {"slot": "main_flow", "audit_ordinal": 0, "content": "The C2 JU, having the capability to originate and report real-time air or surface tracks, performs common tracking in accordance with the correlation and decorrelation procedures and criteria.", "authored_evidence_refs": ["milstd6016b_sec4:P25#C70"], "exposed_evidence_refs": ["milstd6016b_sec4:P23#C64", "milstd6016b_sec4:P25#C68", "milstd6016b_sec4:P39#C126", "milstd6016b_sec4:P113#C379", "milstd6016b_sec4:P41#C133", "milstd6016b_sec4:P25#C70", "milstd6016b_sec4:P113#C381", "milstd6016b_sec4:P43#C138", "milstd6016b_sec4:P54#C179", "milstd6016b_sec4:P25#C71"], "valid_citation": true}, {"slot": "main_flow", "audit_ordinal": 1, "content": "In common tracking, the C2 JU shares a common track number and shifting R^2 between C2 JUs; each air, surface (maritime), land (ground), and space tracked object is normally reported by one C2 JU while other C2 JUs withhold their reports to prevent cluttering the tactical plot.", "authored_evidence_refs": ["milstd6016b_sec4:P25#C68"], "exposed_evidence_refs": ["milstd6016b_sec4:P23#C64", "milstd6016b_sec4:P25#C68", "milstd6016b_sec4:P39#C126", "milstd6016b_sec4:P113#C379", "milstd6016b_sec4:P41#C133", "milstd6016b_sec4:P25#C70", "milstd6016b_sec4:P113#C381", "milstd6016b_sec4:P43#C138", "milstd6016b_sec4:P54#C179", "milstd6016b_sec4:P25#C71"], "valid_citation": true}, {"slot": "main_flow", "audit_ordinal": 2, "content": "The C2 JU commences the correlation process by comparing locally derived sensor data (position, velocity, and altitude) with data received on the interface to prevent or eliminate dual designations.", "authored_evidence_refs": ["milstd6016b_sec4:P25#C71"], "exposed_evidence_refs": ["milstd6016b_sec4:P23#C64", "milstd6016b_sec4:P25#C68", "milstd6016b_sec4:P39#C126", "milstd6016b_sec4:P113#C379", "milstd6016b_sec4:P41#C133", "milstd6016b_sec4:P25#C70", "milstd6016b_sec4:P113#C381", "milstd6016b_sec4:P43#C138", "milstd6016b_sec4:P54#C179", "milstd6016b_sec4:P25#C71"], "valid_citation": true}, {"slot": "main_flow", "audit_ordinal": 3, "content": "The C2 JU periodically compares remote tracks to local tracks (and, optionally, to common local tracks) to determine if a dual designation has occurred.", "authored_evidence_refs": ["milstd6016b_sec4:P113#C379"], "exposed_evidence_refs": ["milstd6016b_sec4:P23#C64", "milstd6016b_sec4:P25#C68", "milstd6016b_sec4:P39#C126", "milstd6016b_sec4:P113#C379", "milstd6016b_sec4:P41#C133", "milstd6016b_sec4:P25#C70", "milstd6016b_sec4:P113#C381", "milstd6016b_sec4:P43#C138", "milstd6016b_sec4:P54#C179", "milstd6016b_sec4:P25#C71"], "valid_citation": true}, {"slot": "main_flow", "audit_ordinal": 4, "content": "When the C2 JU recognizes that two tracks being reported to the interface are eligible for correlation, it initiates action, either automatically or manually.", "authored_evidence_refs": ["milstd6016b_sec4:P113#C379"], "exposed_evidence_refs": ["milstd6016b_sec4:P23#C64", "milstd6016b_sec4:P25#C68", "milstd6016b_sec4:P39#C126", "milstd6016b_sec4:P113#C379", "milstd6016b_sec4:P41#C133", "milstd6016b_sec4:P25#C70", "milstd6016b_sec4:P113#C381", "milstd6016b_sec4:P43#C138", "milstd6016b_sec4:P54#C179", "milstd6016b_sec4:P25#C71"], "valid_citation": true}, {"slot": "main_flow", "audit_ordinal": 5, "content": "The C2 JU reports Air surveillance data using the J3.2 (PTI = 1) message and Surface (Maritime) surveillance data using the J3.3 (PTI = 1) message.", "authored_evidence_refs": ["milstd6016b_sec4:P23#C64"], "exposed_evidence_refs": ["milstd6016b_sec4:P23#C64", "milstd6016b_sec4:P25#C68", "milstd6016b_sec4:P39#C126", "milstd6016b_sec4:P113#C379", "milstd6016b_sec4:P41#C133", "milstd6016b_sec4:P25#C70", "milstd6016b_sec4:P113#C381", "milstd6016b_sec4:P43#C138", "milstd6016b_sec4:P54#C179", "milstd6016b_sec4:P25#C71"], "valid_citation": true}, {"slot": "main_flow", "audit_ordinal": 6, "content": "For Air surveillance reporting, the C2 JU includes Altitude and Altitude Source when available.", "authored_evidence_refs": ["milstd6016b_sec4:P41#C133"], "exposed_evidence_refs": ["milstd6016b_sec4:P23#C64", "milstd6016b_sec4:P25#C68", "milstd6016b_sec4:P39#C126", "milstd6016b_sec4:P113#C379", "milstd6016b_sec4:P41#C133", "milstd6016b_sec4:P25#C70", "milstd6016b_sec4:P113#C381", "milstd6016b_sec4:P43#C138", "milstd6016b_sec4:P54#C179", "milstd6016b_sec4:P25#C71"], "valid_citation": true}, {"slot": "main_flow", "audit_ordinal": 7, "content": "The C2 JU reports the velocity of Air and Surface (Maritime) tracks as course and speed, with speed reported in data miles per hour of ground speed and course reported in degrees with respect to true north.", "authored_evidence_refs": ["milstd6016b_sec4:P43#C138"], "exposed_evidence_refs": ["milstd6016b_sec4:P23#C64", "milstd6016b_sec4:P25#C68", "milstd6016b_sec4:P39#C126", "milstd6016b_sec4:P113#C379", "milstd6016b_sec4:P41#C133", "milstd6016b_sec4:P25#C70", "milstd6016b_sec4:P113#C381", "milstd6016b_sec4:P43#C138", "milstd6016b_sec4:P54#C179", "milstd6016b_sec4:P25#C71"], "valid_citation": true}, {"slot": "main_flow", "audit_ordinal": 8, "content": "The C2 JU exchanges track identity as defined in paragraph 4.4.2.1.", "authored_evidence_refs": ["milstd6016b_sec4:P43#C138"], "exposed_evidence_refs": ["milstd6016b_sec4:P23#C64", "milstd6016b_sec4:P25#C68", "milstd6016b_sec4:P39#C126", "milstd6016b_sec4:P113#C379", "milstd6016b_sec4:P41#C133", "milstd6016b_sec4:P25#C70", "milstd6016b_sec4:P113#C381", "milstd6016b_sec4:P43#C138", "milstd6016b_sec4:P54#C179", "milstd6016b_sec4:P25#C71"], "valid_citation": true}, {"slot": "alternative_flow", "audit_ordinal": 0, "content": "At main flow step 0, the C2 JU may also perform manual decorrelation, and may have a capability to require manual confirmation of automatic decorrelations.", "authored_evidence_refs": ["milstd6016b_sec4:P39#C126"], "exposed_evidence_refs": ["milstd6016b_sec4:P41#C133", "milstd6016b_sec4:P23#C64", "milstd6016b_sec4:P39#C126", "milstd6016b_sec4:P113#C379", "milstd6016b_sec4:P47#C154", "milstd6016b_sec4:P113#C381", "milstd6016b_sec4:P25#C68", "milstd6016b_sec4:P25#C70", "milstd6016b_sec4:P43#C138", "milstd6016b_sec4:P53#C177"], "valid_citation": true}, {"slot": "alternative_flow", "audit_ordinal": 1, "content": "At main flow step 4, if a correlation request is rejected, the C2 JU transmits the J7.2 message with the RV field set to value 2 to report the rejection. When the RV field is set to value 3, it indicates the correlation was manually initiated and shall be accepted unless certain conditions apply which require rejection.", "authored_evidence_refs": ["milstd6016b_sec4:P113#C381"], "exposed_evidence_refs": ["milstd6016b_sec4:P41#C133", "milstd6016b_sec4:P23#C64", "milstd6016b_sec4:P39#C126", "milstd6016b_sec4:P113#C379", "milstd6016b_sec4:P47#C154", "milstd6016b_sec4:P113#C381", "milstd6016b_sec4:P25#C68", "milstd6016b_sec4:P25#C70", "milstd6016b_sec4:P43#C138", "milstd6016b_sec4:P53#C177"], "valid_citation": true}, {"slot": "alternative_flow", "audit_ordinal": 2, "content": "At main flow step 5, if the C2 JU does not have R^2, it is responsible for monitoring IFF/SIF surveillance data and only reporting if it holds different data with the J7.5 message; the JU with R^2 reports all IFF/SIF valid data locally held for that track in accordance with the transmit rules for the J3 messages.", "authored_evidence_refs": ["milstd6016b_sec4:P47#C154"], "exposed_evidence_refs": ["milstd6016b_sec4:P41#C133", "milstd6016b_sec4:P23#C64", "milstd6016b_sec4:P39#C126", "milstd6016b_sec4:P113#C379", "milstd6016b_sec4:P47#C154", "milstd6016b_sec4:P113#C381", "milstd6016b_sec4:P25#C68", "milstd6016b_sec4:P25#C70", "milstd6016b_sec4:P43#C138", "milstd6016b_sec4:P53#C177"], "valid_citation": true}, {"slot": "alternative_flow", "audit_ordinal": 3, "content": "At main flow step 5, if the C2 JU ceases reporting a track for which it currently has R^2, it transmits the J7.0 (ACT = 0) message, except when it ceases reporting because it has relinquished R^2 to another JU or when that track becomes an Active IU on the network with the same TN.", "authored_evidence_refs": ["milstd6016b_sec4:P53#C177"], "exposed_evidence_refs": ["milstd6016b_sec4:P41#C133", "milstd6016b_sec4:P23#C64", "milstd6016b_sec4:P39#C126", "milstd6016b_sec4:P113#C379", "milstd6016b_sec4:P47#C154", "milstd6016b_sec4:P113#C381", "milstd6016b_sec4:P25#C68", "milstd6016b_sec4:P25#C70", "milstd6016b_sec4:P43#C138", "milstd6016b_sec4:P53#C177"], "valid_citation": true}, {"slot": "exception_flow", "audit_ordinal": 0, "content": "If a correlation request is rejected, the J7.2 message with the RV field set to value 2 shall be transmitted to report the rejection. Exit: the rejection is reported via J7.2.", "authored_evidence_refs": ["milstd6016b_sec4:P113#C381"], "exposed_evidence_refs": ["milstd6016b_sec4:P39#C126", "milstd6016b_sec4:P113#C381", "milstd6016b_sec4:P23#C64", "milstd6016b_sec4:P113#C379", "milstd6016b_sec4:P41#C133", "milstd6016b_sec4:P25#C70", "milstd6016b_sec4:P25#C71", "milstd6016b_sec4:P25#C68", "milstd6016b_sec4:P54#C179", "milstd6016b_sec4:P47#C154"], "valid_citation": true}, {"slot": "exception_flow", "audit_ordinal": 1, "content": "After initially achieving Active status, or after returning to Active status from Inactive status or TDS Failure, C2 JUs capable of assuming R^2 for air, surface, or land tracks shall not transmit air, surface, or land tracks until sufficient reporting responsibility checks, correlation, and data registration are performed; the minimum wait before reporting air and surface tracks is 12 seconds. Exit: transmission is withheld until those checks and the minimum wait are complete.", "authored_evidence_refs": ["milstd6016b_sec4:P54#C179"], "exposed_evidence_refs": ["milstd6016b_sec4:P39#C126", "milstd6016b_sec4:P113#C381", "milstd6016b_sec4:P23#C64", "milstd6016b_sec4:P113#C379", "milstd6016b_sec4:P41#C133", "milstd6016b_sec4:P25#C70", "milstd6016b_sec4:P25#C71", "milstd6016b_sec4:P25#C68", "milstd6016b_sec4:P54#C179", "milstd6016b_sec4:P47#C154"], "valid_citation": true}, {"slot": "exception_flow", "audit_ordinal": 2, "content": "For IFF/SIF surveillance data reporting, all JUs without R^2 are responsible for monitoring such data and only reporting if they hold different data with the J7.5 message. Exit: if different data are held, report them with J7.5; otherwise continue monitoring and do not report.", "authored_evidence_refs": ["milstd6016b_sec4:P47#C154"], "exposed_evidence_refs": ["milstd6016b_sec4:P39#C126", "milstd6016b_sec4:P113#C381", "milstd6016b_sec4:P23#C64", "milstd6016b_sec4:P113#C379", "milstd6016b_sec4:P41#C133", "milstd6016b_sec4:P25#C70", "milstd6016b_sec4:P25#C71", "milstd6016b_sec4:P25#C68", "milstd6016b_sec4:P54#C179", "milstd6016b_sec4:P47#C154"], "valid_citation": true}, {"slot": "postconditions", "audit_ordinal": 0, "content": "Air surveillance data is reported using the J3.2 (PTI = 1) message.", "authored_evidence_refs": ["milstd6016b_sec4:P23#C64"], "exposed_evidence_refs": ["milstd6016b_sec4:P39#C126", "milstd6016b_sec4:P23#C64", "milstd6016b_sec4:P113#C381", "milstd6016b_sec4:P54#C179", "milstd6016b_sec4:P25#C70", "milstd6016b_sec4:P43#C138", "milstd6016b_sec4:P25#C71", "milstd6016b_sec4:P53#C177", "milstd6016b_sec4:P113#C379", "milstd6016b_sec4:P41#C133"], "valid_citation": true}, {"slot": "postconditions", "audit_ordinal": 1, "content": "Surface (Maritime) surveillance data is reported using the J3.3 (PTI = 1) message.", "authored_evidence_refs": ["milstd6016b_sec4:P23#C64"], "exposed_evidence_refs": ["milstd6016b_sec4:P39#C126", "milstd6016b_sec4:P23#C64", "milstd6016b_sec4:P113#C381", "milstd6016b_sec4:P54#C179", "milstd6016b_sec4:P25#C70", "milstd6016b_sec4:P43#C138", "milstd6016b_sec4:P25#C71", "milstd6016b_sec4:P53#C177", "milstd6016b_sec4:P113#C379", "milstd6016b_sec4:P41#C133"], "valid_citation": true}, {"slot": "postconditions", "audit_ordinal": 2, "content": "Air surveillance reporting includes Altitude and Altitude Source when available.", "authored_evidence_refs": ["milstd6016b_sec4:P41#C133"], "exposed_evidence_refs": ["milstd6016b_sec4:P39#C126", "milstd6016b_sec4:P23#C64", "milstd6016b_sec4:P113#C381", "milstd6016b_sec4:P54#C179", "milstd6016b_sec4:P25#C70", "milstd6016b_sec4:P43#C138", "milstd6016b_sec4:P25#C71", "milstd6016b_sec4:P53#C177", "milstd6016b_sec4:P113#C379", "milstd6016b_sec4:P41#C133"], "valid_citation": true}, {"slot": "postconditions", "audit_ordinal": 3, "content": "The velocity of Air and Surface (Maritime) tracks is reported as course and speed, with speed reported in data miles per hour of ground speed and course reported in degrees with respect to true north.", "authored_evidence_refs": ["milstd6016b_sec4:P43#C138"], "exposed_evidence_refs": ["milstd6016b_sec4:P39#C126", "milstd6016b_sec4:P23#C64", "milstd6016b_sec4:P113#C381", "milstd6016b_sec4:P54#C179", "milstd6016b_sec4:P25#C70", "milstd6016b_sec4:P43#C138", "milstd6016b_sec4:P25#C71", "milstd6016b_sec4:P53#C177", "milstd6016b_sec4:P113#C379", "milstd6016b_sec4:P41#C133"], "valid_citation": true}, {"slot": "postconditions", "audit_ordinal": 4, "content": "Track identity is exchanged as defined in paragraph 4.4.2.1.", "authored_evidence_refs": ["milstd6016b_sec4:P43#C138"], "exposed_evidence_refs": ["milstd6016b_sec4:P39#C126", "milstd6016b_sec4:P23#C64", "milstd6016b_sec4:P113#C381", "milstd6016b_sec4:P54#C179", "milstd6016b_sec4:P25#C70", "milstd6016b_sec4:P43#C138", "milstd6016b_sec4:P25#C71", "milstd6016b_sec4:P53#C177", "milstd6016b_sec4:P113#C379", "milstd6016b_sec4:P41#C133"], "valid_citation": true}], "empty_slots": [], "material_sha256": "78f66f35d3cb4410694f8a7edabfd267f5f018d01d6001da3df4b37dea477192"};
